    <item>
      <title>Material themed cards</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/components/material-themed-cards/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 09 Jun 2021 10:39:16 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/components/material-themed-cards/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;These cards are meant to be themed using only the following variables:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;  --primary-hue: 265;&#xA;  --primary-saturation: 90%;&#xA;  --primary-lightness: 47%;&#xA;&#xA;  --surface: white;&#xA;  --background: white;&#xA;  --card-text: #424242;&#xA;  --body-text: #424242;&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;It works with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.w3schools.com/colors/colors_hsl.asp&#34;&gt;HSL colors&lt;/a&gt;, by inputting the &lt;code&gt;--primary-hue&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--primary-saturation&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--primary-lightness&lt;/code&gt; separately.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These cards can be used anywhere and will fit 100% of their parent container. We recommend using them with a grid system, like the one used here.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;All cards are prented with a sticky filter bar, to present how they can interact. The sticky bar is compatible with the color theming, but is not required.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
